 trailer for nba 2k 22 along  with a deep dive blog post that's  explaining all of the big changes that's  coming to the gameplay this year in  short 2k says its goal for nba 2k 22 was  to deliver faster paced gameplay more  responsive player movement and more  skill based offensive abilities starting  with shooting nba 2k 22 has a number of  changes the most obvious of which is its  new shot meter that now has a  dynamically resizing make window that  expands when you're taking high quality  shots with good shooters but will shrink  when heavily contested using a low rated  shooter or fatigued ultimately rewarding  players for taking smarter opportunities  thanks to a revamped blocking system  defenders will make it more difficult to  finish a play with a flashy dunk there  are also timing meters for alley-oops  and skill dunk attempts but only on new  generation consoles  on defense 2k said it has rebuilt the  shot contest and blocking systems and  thanks to this players will now see  snatch blocks and volleyball spikes that  weren't in previous games while also  delivering some improvements to steals  with a greater focus on specific players  steel attributes  nba 2k 22's september 10th release date  is coming up very soon and there was  even more gameplay details revealed  besides what i already mentioned so if  you want to see the entire list of all  the changes and updates then be sure to  head on over to gamesbot.com  lots of first looks kicking off this  week as we saw welcome to raccoon city  and dead space and tomorrow we are going  to get our first look at new marvel  midnight sun's gameplay right here on  our channel so make sure you come back  thanks so much for watching and we'll  see you next time  [Music]  you
 

